      "statement": "Identify the error:\n\"I was **looking for (A)** my cat all day, and I finally **found out (B)** it **hiding (C)** under the **sofa (D)**.\"",
      "context": "Identifying errors in phrasal verb usage.",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "looking for",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect. Correct use for searching."
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "found out",
          "is_correct": true,
          "feedback": "Correct! Error found. \"Found out\" means discovering information. For finding a physical object, we just use \"found\"."
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "hiding",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
